Z||000000||frontal lobe||03-22-2000||03:36 PM||||This story is fiero related because it happened in the fiero.  I'm going off to work and I'm taking my briefcase because it makes me look intelligent (I think, anyway) but really all it has in it is the sports page of the day's newspaper, my latest edition of car and driver, and a few 2 month old work papers.  I also put a can of diet mountain dew in it (no more 2 liter bottles for me, and they don't fit anyway), shut the briefcase, heard a little puff of air as the air got squeezed out of the case, and loaded us into the fiero.<P>I get to the parking lot at work, grab my briefcase, get out of the car and start to walk in.  I look down and my right thigh is all wet!  Control problems?  Not again!  But wait.  My briefcase is leaking green fluid.  ATF leak?  No, my briefcase is a manual.<P>OH NO!!  The puff of fluid must have been the mountain dew can.  Sure enough, I open the briefcase and the cheap can has a tiny pin hole in it and leaked into my briefcase.<BR>Fortunately, everything dried out AND no leakage on the fiero seats.  Phew.<P>Just passing this warning on to any briefcase-toting fiero owners.||||reg||1
